# Shared settings of every dns-* TLS mode (imported inside the `tls { ... }` block).
#
# resolvers: public resolvers check the challenge record, so a local or split-horizon DNS (the A record of the
# subdomain points to a LAN address) cannot get in the way.
# dns_challenge_override_domain: where the TXT record is written. The default _acme-challenge.<domain> is exactly
# what Caddy would use anyway; set FLOWSTUDIO_DNS_CHALLENGE_DOMAIN when _acme-challenge is delegated by CNAME to
# another zone (for example a provider without a Caddy module, such as Hostpoint or cyon, delegating to deSEC).
resolvers {$FLOWSTUDIO_DNS_RESOLVERS}
dns_challenge_override_domain {$FLOWSTUDIO_DNS_CHALLENGE_DOMAIN}
